    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 oral exposure records for quaternary ammonium antimuscarinics show only pg/mL-level plasma concentrations after oral dosing (trospium 60 mg ER Cmax ~1.5-1.9 ng/mL and AUC24 ~23 ng·h/mL; glycopyrronium 2 mg oral Cmax 318 pg/mL; scopolamine 0.5 mg oral AUC0-24 50.77 ng·min/mL), consistent with poor oral absorption.",
      "card_ids": ["C72", "C85", "C111", "C98", "C87", "C97"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 C119 reports trospium chloride solubility >100 mg/mL, indicating high aqueous solubility for a quaternary ammonium antimuscarinic; this shows solubility is not the limiting factor but provides no permeability or F evidence for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C119"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Permeability records for other compounds (e.g., fexofenadine human/rat Peff, C138/C165) are not directly transferable to the query and do not provide affirmative F≥20% evidence.",
      "card_ids": ["C138", "C165"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "intestinal_absorption_permeability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C119"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No query-specific measured oral bioavailability, permeability, or solubility data are supplied.",
    "L4 records are predominantly for other molecules; no direct permeability measurement for N-butylscopolamine or a quaternary ammonium analog is provided.",
    "C119 is a solubility measurement only; it does not provide permeability or F for trospium.",
    "L3 exposure records lack IV comparators, so absolute F cannot be derived from them.",
    "No formulation, dose, or species match for the query is available."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Prediction remains low. The query is N-butylscopolamine, a permanently charged quaternary ammonium tropane ester; transferable L1 evidence from umeclidinium (negligible/low oral F, ≤12% systemic availability) and oxybutynin (~7% absolute F) supports F <20%. L3 oral exposure records for quaternary ammonium antimuscarinics show only pg/mL-level plasma concentrations after oral dosing. L4 adds trospium solubility >100 mg/mL, indicating solubility is not limiting, but provides no permeability or F evidence for the query; no L4 record affirmatively supports F ≥20%. Confidence remains high."
}

